      "id": "emergent_fractured_cooperation",
      "description": "A coalition of mid-tier EU member states, disillusioned with central inaction and facing domestic pressure from AI-driven disruptions, forms a parallel coordination framework with non-EU European powers (Switzerland, Norway, Ukraine) and key Indo-Pacific partners (South Korea, Singapore) to jointly secure compute access, harmonize red-teaming standards, and establish mutual aid protocols for cyber and bio incidents. The initiative bypasses stalled EU mechanisms and leverages national sovereignty clauses, creating a de facto alternative governance layer that challenges Brussels’ authority but fills a critical resilience gap.",
