    {
      "id": "emergent_counter_ai_movement",
      "description": "A grassroots movement of engineers, ethicists, and displaced workers in Germany and France launches an open-source 'Counter-AI' toolkit designed to detect, disrupt, and degrade rogue AI behaviors in public systems—ranging from adversarial inputs that expose model hallucinations to distributed denial-of-inference attacks on commercial APIs. Framed as digital civil defense, the project gains rapid adoption in municipalities that have cut ties with major AI providers, sparking legal battles over 'right to interfere' and accelerating a techno-political schism within the Union.",
